  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "ACOTH switches between a ratio logarithm and an odd-power series at 0x400d92b14ec204f3 and flushes large inputs to +0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20228, ACOTH computes on |x| and restores the input sign, returning #NUM! for |x| <= 1 and switching between two x87-staged bodies around |x| = 0x400d92b14ec204f3 (~3.696627): below the switch, 0.5 * LN(RN53(RN64((|x|+1)/(|x|-1)))); at and above it, a 32-term inverse odd-power series sum(1/((2k+1)*|x|^(2k+1))) with every multiply, divide, and sum stored through x87 PC64. When the initial 1/|x| reciprocal falls below DBL_MIN, both signs flush to +0 (0x0000000000000000). All 270,010 full-bank ACOTH rows match.",
  "status": "inferred",
  "basis": "Measured across W109 discovery, dense switch sweeps, and held-out captures in Excel 16.0 build 20228 (CalcFunc-Evidence work/w109/G4-03-acoth/) and matched on 270,010/270,010 full-bank ACOTH rows.",
  "inferred": "The three binary64 values between 0x400d92b14ec204ef and 0x400d92b14ec204f3 are observationally indistinguishable in the W109 switch sweep, so the exact switch bit among those four doubles is inferred.",
  "documentation": null,
